From ac345f1c0cf402a9c26363f675196fab32c8bd8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:17:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(post): return the rotaries to zero at program end
 (Fanuc, Doosan DNM)

A program whose last section is tilted ended with the table or the head
at the last tilt after M30. The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now end such
a program with the same blocks as the return of #3466: G49, the Z
retract, G90, the zero angle words with no X/Y word, then an
incremental X/Y home (G91 G28 X0 Y0) and M30. Doosan unclamps (M11)
and clamps (M10) a turning A around the return. With safeRetract G53
the program writes G53 Z, then the zero angles. An upright program
ends byte for byte as before.

The catalog program multiaxis/indexed changes in its last blocks only.

Fixes #3540

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
